WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.850
"IDOLiSH7 Regular Namesake Show (Temp)"

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.850
There's going to be an IDOLiSH7 
regular namesake show!

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:07.230
Once our namesake show begins airing, 
we'll receive offers from other places.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.820
And tomorrow is Re:vale's show.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.990
Seize the opportunity and climb up here.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.520
Discover...

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.500
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.660
There's a glimmer I want 
to realize with you

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:29.730
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.070
Wow...

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.690
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.780
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.530
No matter what tomorrow's like,
 it won't betray us

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:01.240
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.850
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.390
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:11.880
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.420
Discover...

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.220
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.850
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.160
Night sky

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.100
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.500
There's a glimmer I want 
to realize with you

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:36.150
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.450
Wow...

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.000
#02 Wavering Feelings

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.260
Zero Arena's inaugural show...

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.030
You think we can perform in it?

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.510
It'd be amazing if we did, right?

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.290
Will the groups be selected by audition?

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.430
I don't really get it, but 
Re:vale are nice guys.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.520
They said they'd recommend us.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.460
That experience reminded 
me how amazing Re:vale is.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.990
They're friendly, kind, and treat 
their guests and staff well.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.990
They're not just cool on the 
outside, but on the inside, too.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.060
Mr. Momo and Yuki were 
charming gentlemen.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.500
No wonder they're top stars.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.800
You're right. I'm glad we got 
to meet such great seniors.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.540
There you are.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.170
Hey!

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:37.270
Yuki-san.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:38.170
Momo-san.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.740
What's going on?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.860
Yamato-kun, I'd like to 
discuss something with you.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.170
Are you free after this?

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.680
Actually, I'm busy.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.180
What?!

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.500
Y-You really should talk
 to him, shouldn't you?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.330
After all, they were so hospitable to us.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.940
He's right. You have plenty of time.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.420
They're busy, though.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.700
Besides, they're just 
trying to be diplomatic.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.430
I should get going, Senpai.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.200
W-Wait, Yamato-san!

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.150
I'm sorry, Yuki-san.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:08.540
Please excuse us.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.580
Okay.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.100
Thank you so much for today.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.580
Thank you.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.000
If the opportunity comes up again, 
we'd appreciate your consideration.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.350
Later.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.550
Thank you for today.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.190
Sure thing. Thanks!

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.770
Thank you.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.680
He turned me down.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.770
It's that kid with the glasses?

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.310
Yeah. He's grown so much.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:34.170
The first time we met, he was 
wearing a school uniform.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:35.610
A blazer?

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.490
Standing collar, actually.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.450
He's a ball of misanthropy.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.450
He saw celebrities as 
less than cockroaches.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.730
Yamato-san, are you sure about this?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.330
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.800
I thought you were acquaintances.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.510
I've heard you have many 
acquaintances in the industry—

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.840
Shut up!

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.070
What?

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.280
You shouldn't bring that up.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.840
It's way better that you don't.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.350
Why are you guys reacting so strangely?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.150
Because...

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:16.610
Whenever we talk about this, 
it puts you in a terrible mood.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.370
Really? You guys were worried about that?

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.990
I'm really <i>so</i> sorry.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.990
It's fine...

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.740
Yamato-san, don't tease 
people younger than you.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.150
Sometimes you lack composure

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.980
and can be childish, y'know?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.620
Mitsu, aren't you too young to 
be talking about being an adult?

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.830
I became an adult a long time ago!

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.830
Wanna see the photos from 
my coming-of-age ceremony?!

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.010
They're really cute.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.010
Shut up!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.510
Yamato.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.310
What?

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.130
Please remove your glasses.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:52.620
No way. It's not like it'll turn me into 
a pretty girl like in some anime.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.890
Manager, what are we going to 
do about the inaugural show?

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.980
If we receive an offer,

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.650
it'll be IDOLiSH7's biggest job 
since the group's formation.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.670
IDOLiSH7's name would be carved 
into the history of Zero Arena,

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.500
the holy land of the 
legendary idol Zero.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.790
Yes. Yes.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.490
Thank you for contacting me.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:17.290
Goodbye.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.210
What did they say?

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:23.740
Zero Arena's general manager will 
be coming to an IDOLiSH7 concert.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.340
The general manager's 
coming to our show?

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.370
That's amazing.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.940
Well, we've got nothing to lose—

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.410
Let's give this our all!

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:37.060
If we're chosen, we get to perform 
alongside Re:vale and TRIGGER.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.940
We'll be giving it our all, then.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.670
Speaking of Zero Arena's general manager,

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:45.400
I've heard he has high standards 
for stage direction as well.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.950
You'll be handling the stage direction 
of our next concert, too, right?

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.700
You've got a good reputation.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.060
I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.450
Not to put pressure on you, but...

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.530
This performance relies 
heavily on your skills,

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.060
so make sure you do a good job.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:00.880
O-Okay...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.590
You're pressuring the crap out of her, man.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.300
Manager, if you'd like, I'll lend
 you my Zero concert DVDs.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.010
I think they'd help inspire you.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.970
You'll be so moved by them.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.850
Thank you.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.390
Um... I'll do my very best!

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:30.090
Wow. I feel like I'm being sucked 
deeper and deeper into Zero's world.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.780
I wonder who directed this?

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.040
The stage director is...

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.650
Haw9?

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.040
Yes?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.760
Can I come in?

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:41.790
Sure.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.700
Excuse the intrusion.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.590
What is it, Dad? Are you hungry?

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.340
Are you watching the DVDs you 
borrowed from Mitsuki-kun?

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.220
Zero really is amazing.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.810
He's truly wonderful!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:57.330
I've seen him numerous 
times on TV before,

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.350
but ever since I started this job,

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.710
I'm discovering tons of new
things when I watch him.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:06.480
Zero's concerts had a unique flavor
 that you couldn't get anywhere else.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.810
I'd like to meet this Haw9 
person who directed his shows.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:12.570
I wonder if it's possible 
to get in touch with him.

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.140
It'll be difficult.

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:20.210
Once Zero disappeared, I stopped
 hearing his name, too.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.710
I see.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:25.700
On the other hand, he left 
us these fantastic shows.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:28.510
You should learn everything 
you can from them.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.420
Yes, sir!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.260
No, wait, I mean Dad.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.760
It feels like we're at the office.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.940
Oh, right.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.850
It's almost Banri-kun's 
fifth year working for us.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.230
I'm thinking about getting him a present.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.090
Can you think of something?

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:48.140
It's been that long?

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:51.280
Time flies, doesn't it? 
He does a good job.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:56.220
When you were still in school and I saw
you give Banri-kun Valentine's Day chocolates...

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.290
I didn't know what I'd do.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:02.080
That's because he's always 
looking after you.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:06.850
It's important to study, but don't push 
yourself too hard and get some sleep.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:07.850
Goodnight.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.010
Goodnight.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.030
Zero Arena...

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.800
Maybe I'll go there tomorrow.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:28.820
Hi, girl.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.180
Nagi-san!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.950
Where are you going?

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.450
I thought I'd go to Zero Arena for some
inspiration for our stage direction.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.640
Oh! Then I'll go with you.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:41.110
What?

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.580
Let's go on a date.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.250
Zero Arena...

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.510
The holy land of idols where 
Zero performed his last concert.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:56.450
I remember the day 
I danced here with you.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:57.890
You're right.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:02.600
You had tears in your eyes, 
but you were still smiling.

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:06.190
You were so beautiful 
under the starry sky.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:11.490
Oh, no. "Beautiful" is how you'd
 describe someone like you.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.360
You look like a character 
straight out of a story.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.990
Do you feel inspired?

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.000
Why are you laughing?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.650
No reason. That's what 
makes you wonderful.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:35.030
Oh, right. A limited edition <i>Magical 
Cocona</i> planner is going on sale.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:38.160
Oh, yes! It's supremely lovely!

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.100
It comes with special stickers, special 
labels, and a special bookmark!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.020
It's a must-buy!

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.270
Hey!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:47.770
Oh.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.250
Are you all right?

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.740
Yes. Thank you.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.220
You dropped this.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.610
Sorry. Thank you.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.660
<i>Stage Direction for Concerts</i>.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.790
You're studying stage direction?

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.960
Yes—

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.210
Hey, Kinako!

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.550
What a funny rabbit.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:20.470
It's like they're trying to dance 
while looking at Zero Arena.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.770
It's been 15 years since Zero vanished.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:29.650
So many idols have performed 
there at Zero Arena.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:34.980
And so many idols have disappeared 
while dreaming of standing on that stage,

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.990
just like that rabbit.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:40.580
Who are you? Do you like idols?

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:44.370
Yes. Idols, the fans who dream of idols,

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.500
and the staff that put a bow on those dreams.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.870
The staff that put a bow on those dreams?

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:53.060
Stage direction is one such job.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:58.790
The singing and dancing of idols 
moves the hearts of audiences.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:04.550
When combined with the right direction, 
the audience is even more moved.

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:07.890
Their eyes glitter as though 
a spell has been cast on them.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:12.120
I used to train idols once.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.860
I was also a stage director.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.270
Really?

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.930
Yes. Those were such fun days.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:24.710
I wanted to tell the entire world about
 the charm of the idols only I knew.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:25.780
I know what you mean.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:31.110
I cheered them on so my personal 
stars would reach the starry sky.

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:34.310
I supported them so they 
could reach beyond rainbows.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.250
I know what you mean!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:39.360
I feel exactly the same way, as I'm 
supporting a group of idols right now!

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.970
I see. What a coincidence.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:45.140
Work hard. Make your 
wonderful stars glow.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:49.650
Thanks. Your words make my heart leap.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.660
She's currently studying stage direction.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.530
Do you have any advice for her?

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:01.030
The trick to stage direction is 
to know the appeal of your idols.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.860
To know their appeal?

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.950
To become more engrossed in idols than anyone else

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:09.060
while also dissecting them
 more intensely than anyone else.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:13.460
Do that, and you'll see the 
colors that make them shine.

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.540
Light or darkness?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.420
Red lights or blue lights?

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:22.340
Show and hide.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:25.220
Tantalize and parade!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.800
Flashes and lasers!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.560
Disco balls!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:32.180
Quiet sections and flashy sections!

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.060
The set list is stairs 
to a magical castle!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:42.070
Before the clock strikes 12, 
cast a spell on the audience!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.570
On nights when pumpkins transform 
into carriages, what do idols become?

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.340
They become glittering 
dreams themselves!

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:55.830
Smiles dance, happiness bursts, 
and souls step to the beat!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:13:00.730
The cheers that shower down on 
them envelop the idols in light!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.150
Idols, fans, and the staff 
share the greatest moment

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:08.500
and emotion that will 
never be seen again!

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.310
As though partaking in the miracle 
that exists only in this place...

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:22.570
It seems this rabbit likes idols, too.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.320
That was wonderful!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.690
I felt like I was 
performing in a concert!

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:29.820
Me, too!

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:34.660
I think I understand a little of what's
 important to stage direction.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:36.790
That's good.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:41.200
Sorry for taking so much 
of your time. I should go.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.840
Good luck with your studies.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.510
Wait! Excuse me—

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.150
He's gone.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:54.890
Cast a spell...

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:03.740
I've completed the set list 
and stage set for the concert.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.070
Thanks. What's it like?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.370
I've prepared documents.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:11.530
Later, while reviewing the choreography,

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.120
I'd like to explain the 
overall flow of the show.

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:16.130
This sounds like it should be good.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:19.440
Yes. I received a hint 
from a certain person.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:20.380
A certain person?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.000
Someone I met at Zero Arena.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.930
He said he'd trained idols before 
and done stage direction work.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:32.250
He's the manager's master instructor 
who we happened to meet.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.630
You're right.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.350
So it was a once-in-a-lifetime encounter?

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:40.130
Like buying strawberries for one yen?

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.110
I don't think that's the same thing.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.090
Let's give this concert our all!

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:45.820
If we catch the eye of the general manager,

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.990
then we can sing on the 
stage that Zero stood on.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.810
I hope we can meet Re:vale's expectations.

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:53.990
We'll do our best not to put 
your stage direction to waste.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.430
Thank you.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:15:01.420
IDOLiSH7 is a special gift all your 
fans are excitedly waiting for.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.690
By wrapping it in great direction,

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:06.620
I'll draw out your appeal 
as much as possible.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.180
I'll do my best to present 
you to the audience.

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:15.680
This is crazy!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.980
I'm so excited for this concert! 
It's been forever!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.030
Hey, look.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.120
All right!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:48.000
There's a lot riding on today's concert.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:52.100
Whatever we try achieve, 
whatever we aim for...

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:55.180
For us, there's only one shortest route.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.850
Let's give this everything 
we've got right now!

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.850
All right, let's go!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.290
Yeah!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.550
<b>Izumi Iori</b>

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.280
<i>The magic is starting.</i>

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:31.290
(Hey! Girl! We are S, E, V, E, N…

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.290
Here we go!!!)

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:43.810
(Stand up! Hands up!!)

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:50.780
My heart is pounding and I can't stop it

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:55.030
My heart is Throbbing as I wake up

00:16:56.620 --> 00:17:00.410
We can make it, only dream

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.250
We remember distance days,

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:07.910
Memories Melodies

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:28.900
Good evening! We are IDOLiSH7!

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.410
Thank you so much for 
coming to see us today.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:34.570
Are you guys having fun?

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.570
We're having fun!

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:37.570
That's good!

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:42.870
IDOLiSH7's regular show <i>Lovely Night 
With You!</i> will be starting soon.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.610
Congratulations! I'll definitely watch!

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:46.820
We've been waiting for it!

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:48.130
Thank you!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:52.090
Show us your support whether 
we're in concert or on TV.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:55.460
Here's our next song.

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:09.920
Believe in yourself (We can do it!)

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.150
Believe in yourself (We can do it!)

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:15.990
Believe in yourself, 
reach for the dream…

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:19.490
Forcing ourselves to face upwards

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:24.140
The fixed area of the sky

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:27.290
Somehow always seems so vast

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.540
Simmering with impatience

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:32.040
"Just be true to yourself"

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:37.380
The wind softly whispered

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:41.850
We wrote in the blank 
white pages of a notebook

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.610
The trajectory of our future

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:46.770
Let's go and meet it

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:52.400
Anytime we can start running

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:54.020
(In this place that keeps changing)

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:59.350
Raise it up high, our Joker Flag

00:18:59.350 --> 00:19:02.370
We'll clash (and search)

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:04.260
And someday turn into light

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.490
Run quickly

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:12.170
And boldly Kira X Kira 
jump in (all right!)

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:23.430
Come on and dream the greatest 
of dreams Let's fly!

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:27.050
<i>An image of all seven. Solo images.</i>

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.020
Be there!

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.220
Right? Dancing DREAM!!

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:31.450
<i>Five to two. Three to four. Six to one.</i>

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.450
Even farther away...

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:34.150
<i>Going through countless silhouettes.</i>

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:35.280
Yes Dancing BEAT!! Even farther away

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:38.500
<i>Matching the melody by coming 
together or spreading out.</i>

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.500
Night and day!! I want to deliver

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:44.990
Never knowing what it means to 
stand still keep charging ahead

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.420
<i>Iori-san's perfection.</i>

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.180
<i>Yamato-san's acting ability.</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.210
<i>Mitsuki-san's energy.</i>

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.930
Right? Dancing BEAT!! 
An even more wonderful

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.470
<i>Tamaki-san's powerful dancing.</i>

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:52.140
Night and day!! Thrill

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.000
<i>Sogo-san's gentle silhouette.</i>

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:55.540
We'll search for it together

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:57.000
<i>Nagi-san's elegant gestures.</i>

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:00.340
Our future will be eternally Shining!

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:00.940
<i>And Riku-san's smile and voice
 that everyone loves dearly.</i>

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:06.050
We are the eternal Dreamer!!

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.890
<i>There's no time to close your eyes.</i>

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:09.520
<i>IDOLiSH7 keeps drawing everyone's 
gaze, as though casting a spell.</i>

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:12.950
La la la la... forever wish

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:12.350
What a great space.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:15.250
The singing and dancing is good, too.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:20.150
La la la la...

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.490
And they share a sense 
of unity with their fans.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.150
IDOLiSH7 seems all right.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.470
We're IDOLiSH7!

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:34.750
Thank you for coming tonight, everyone!

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:37.750
Thank you!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:21:17.940
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:42.500
Riku!

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:43.170
Riku-san!

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:48.550
Nanase-san, open your mouth!

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:49.480
You need a nebulizer!

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:51.100
I won't. It'll make me hoarse.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:53.430
The encore—

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:55.970
We can't do an encore, Riku.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:57.690
I can do it.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.990
We'll have to send MEZZO" on.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:02.690
Sogo-san, Tamaki-san.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:04.090
Got it.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:06.320
Don't push yourself, Riku-kun. Promise me.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:09.330
S-Sorry...

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.460
You don't have to apologize.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:14.760
Rikkun, we'll buy you some time.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:15.710
Let's go, So-chan.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:16.330
Yeah.

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:23.890
Riku...

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:25.580
Use the nebulizer!

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:28.590
No. If I use it now, 
I won't be able to focus.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:29.860
Riku-san...

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.100
I made a promise.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:37.290
I promised I'd sing until 
the concert was over.

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:40.620
And the inaugural show—

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.630
Your health is more important!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.130
Please use the nebulizer!

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:47.450
If you won't, I'm taking you
 to the emergency room!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.300
No, we can't waste this chance!

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.100
We don't have a choice.

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:54.460
Restrain Nanase-san. Get the nebulizer.

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:55.330
Iori!

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:57.850
Riku, your health is the top 
priority. You get that, don't you?

00:21:57.850 --> 00:22:00.960
No! I can do it! I can—

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:12.220
I'm home.

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:15.270
I brought you some cake.

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:17.340
You can enjoy some with the little one.

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:20.800
I watched an IDOLiSH7 concert.

00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:23.020
It was a wonderful time.

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:29.570
But unfortunately, their center couldn't 
come onstage during the encore.

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:33.170
<i>(If you get lost, there's a song here)</i>

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:33.470
Do you know why, Tenn?

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:36.200
Yes. I know why, Kujo-san.

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:40.000
<i>(If you get lost, there's a song here)</i>

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:39.070
After all, we're twins.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:45.710
We came to understand 
a brilliant something

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:51.930
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:22:52.550 --> 00:23:04.320
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:10.530
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:16.180
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.620
The sound of the future

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:22.840
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.090
We quietly adorn

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:31.260
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:35.220
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.740
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:44.980
So I always want you by my side

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"The Proposal"</b>
